-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════
-- PAGE 2: RESEARCH MOTIVATION
-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════

TEXT 210 810 "Research Motivation" 14 1 #1a1a1a bold

-- Para 1
TEXT 80 850 "Large language models (LLMs) have achieved remarkable performance across" 10 1 #222222
TEXT 50 866 "many reasoning tasks, yet they consistently fail at spatial reasoning. On the" 10 1 #222222
TEXT 50 882 "ARC-AGI-2 benchmark, frontier models including Claude Opus and GPT-4o score" 10 1 #222222
TEXT 50 898 "between 2% and 5%, while humans achieve over 80% (Chollet, 2025). Mental" 10 1 #222222
TEXT 50 914 "rotation tasks reduce multimodal LLMs to random chance (Srivastava et al.," 10 1 #222222
TEXT 50 930 "2025), and perspective-taking accuracy for GPT-4o is only 27.5% compared" 10 1 #222222
TEXT 50 946 "to human intuitive performance (Yang et al., 2025). This gap persists despite" 10 1 #222222
TEXT 50 962 "massive increases in model scale, multimodal training, and chain-of-thought" 10 1 #222222
TEXT 50 978 "prompting." 10 1 #222222

-- Para 2
TEXT 80 1006 "From a societal perspective, spatial reasoning failures have real" 10 1 #222222
TEXT 50 1022 "consequences: autonomous vehicle misclassifications have caused serious" 10 1 #222222
TEXT 50 1038 "accidents, warehouse robots fail on 35% of manipulation tasks, and no Level" 10 1 #222222
TEXT 50 1054 "4/5 autonomous surgery has been deployed due to spatial reasoning limitations" 10 1 #222222
TEXT 50 1070 "in soft tissue (Yang et al., 2025). Scientifically, this failure is puzzling" 10 1 #222222
TEXT 50 1086 "because LLMs excel at other forms of reasoning -- mathematical proofs, code" 10 1 #222222
TEXT 50 1102 "generation, logical deduction -- but collapse when reasoning requires" 10 1 #222222
TEXT 50 1118 "understanding 3D structure." 10 1 #222222

-- Para 3
TEXT 80 1146 "Current approaches to improving LLM spatial reasoning focus on adding" 10 1 #222222
TEXT 50 1162 "vision modules: SpatialVLA embeds depth as features in vision-language" 10 1 #222222
TEXT 50 1178 "models, and DepthVLA adds depth streams to multimodal architectures." 10 1 #222222
TEXT 50 1194 "However, these approaches increase model complexity and remain tied to visual" 10 1 #222222
TEXT 50 1210 "input. An alternative, under-explored hypothesis is that LLMs may already" 10 1 #222222
TEXT 50 1226 "possess sufficient reasoning capability, but lack an appropriate" 10 1 #222222
TEXT 50 1242 "representation format for spatial information. Larkin and Simon (1987)" 10 1 #222222
TEXT 50 1258 "demonstrated formally that diagrams can make previously intractable problems" 10 1 #222222
TEXT 50 1274 "trivially solvable -- not by adding new information, but by making spatial" 10 1 #222222
TEXT 50 1290 "relationships computationally accessible." 10 1 #222222


-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════
-- RESEARCH QUESTION
-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════

TEXT 218 1330 "Research Question" 14 1 #1a1a1a bold

-- RQ box with subtle background
RECT 60 1360 475 60 0 #f0f4f8 4
LINE 60 1360 60 1420 1 #1a3a5c 3

TEXT 75 1370 "To what extent do text-based depth representations, generated from a" 10 1 #1a1a1a italic
TEXT 75 1386 "voxel domain-specific language, improve large language model performance" 10 1 #1a1a1a italic
TEXT 75 1402 "on spatial reasoning tasks where current models score below 50%?" 10 1 #1a1a1a italic


-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════
-- BACKGROUND
-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════

TEXT 248 1450 "Background" 14 1 #1a1a1a bold

-- Para 1
TEXT 80 1485 "The theoretical foundation for this work comes from Larkin and Simon" 10 1 #222222
TEXT 50 1501 "(1987), who proved that the computational difference between sentential and" 10 1 #222222
TEXT 50 1517 "diagrammatic representations is not informational but structural: diagrams" 10 1 #222222
TEXT 50 1533 "group spatially related information together, enabling perceptual operations" 10 1 #222222
TEXT 50 1549 "that are computationally expensive in text. This principle suggests that" 10 1 #222222
TEXT 50 1565 "converting spatial problems into structured, spatially-organized text could" 10 1 #222222
TEXT 50 1581 "provide similar benefits for LLMs." 10 1 #222222

-- Para 2
TEXT 80 1609 "Recent work has begun exploring spatial intermediates for LLM reasoning." 10 1 #222222
TEXT 50 1625 "The Visualization-of-Thought (VoT) framework demonstrated that generating" 10 1 #222222
TEXT 50 1641 "spatial intermediates (ASCII-like grids) during reasoning improved LLM" 10 1 #222222
TEXT 50 1657 "performance on navigation and tiling tasks (Wei et al., 2024). The" 10 1 #222222
TEXT 50 1673 "Whiteboard-of-Thought (WoT) paradigm showed that a draw-render-perceive" 10 1 #222222
TEXT 50 1689 "loop -- where models generate visual code, render it, and interpret the" 10 1 #222222
TEXT 50 1705 "output -- improved spatial accuracy over pure text reasoning (Xu et al.," 10 1 #222222
TEXT 50 1721 "2024). VoxPoser used LLMs to generate Python code that filled 3D voxel grids" 10 1 #222222
TEXT 50 1737 "with affordance values for robot planning, achieving zero-shot generalization" 10 1 #222222
TEXT 50 1753 "(Huang et al., 2023)." 10 1 #222222

-- Para 3
TEXT 80 1781 "However, no existing system implements a complete closed loop where an" 10 1 #222222
TEXT 50 1797 "LLM writes 3D spatial code, receives text-based depth feedback from a" 10 1 #222222
TEXT 50 1813 "raycasting camera system, verifies its reasoning against the rendered output," 10 1 #222222
TEXT 50 1829 "and iteratively revises -- all without any vision model. The Mind's Eye" 10 1 #222222
TEXT 50 1845 "system, which this proposal aims to evaluate, implements precisely this" 10 1 #222222
TEXT 50 1861 "architecture using VOXI, a voxel description language, paired with a" 10 1 #222222
TEXT 50 1877 "text-based raycaster that produces ASCII depth maps (digits 0-9 representing" 10 1 #222222
TEXT 50 1893 "distance from camera). Figure 1 shows the system architecture and Figure 2" 10 1 #222222
TEXT 50 1909 "shows the 6-angle feedback mechanism." 10 1 #222222


