-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════
-- METHODS
-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════

TEXT 262 2340 "Methods" 14 1 #1a1a1a bold

-- Experimental Design
TEXT 50 2370 "Experimental Design" 12 1 #1a1a1a bold

TEXT 80 2396 "This study employs a 2x2 factorial design with two independent variables:" 10 1 #222222
TEXT 50 2412 "(a) representation type (natural language only vs. natural language augmented" 10 1 #222222
TEXT 50 2428 "with text-based depth matrices) and (b) model capability level (high-capability" 10 1 #222222
TEXT 50 2444 "model: Claude Sonnet vs. lower-capability model: Claude Haiku). The dependent" 10 1 #222222
TEXT 50 2460 "variable is task accuracy (percentage of correctly answered spatial reasoning" 10 1 #222222
TEXT 50 2476 "questions)." 10 1 #222222

-- Datasets
TEXT 50 2510 "Datasets" 12 1 #1a1a1a bold

TEXT 80 2536 "Three existing benchmarks will be used. First, the SpartQA dataset" 10 1 #222222
TEXT 50 2552 "(Mirzaee et al., 2021), consisting of multi-hop spatial reasoning questions" 10 1 #222222
TEXT 50 2568 "derived from natural language scene descriptions. Twenty tasks of varying" 10 1 #222222
TEXT 50 2584 "difficulty will be sampled. Second, the CATER video benchmark (Girdhar &" 10 1 #222222
TEXT 50 2600 "Ramanan, 2020), providing real-world video scenes requiring 3D spatial" 10 1 #222222
TEXT 50 2616 "understanding; five tasks involving object counting, motion tracking, and" 10 1 #222222
TEXT 50 2632 "occlusion detection will be used, with depth matrices extracted at 20x20" 10 1 #222222
TEXT 50 2648 "resolution using Depth Anything V2. Third, thirty automatically generated" 10 1 #222222
TEXT 50 2664 "VOXI scenes (16x16x16 grids, seed=42) with five question types: collision" 10 1 #222222
TEXT 50 2680 "detection, relative position, motion direction, object count, and" 10 1 #222222
TEXT 50 2696 "closer-to-camera judgments." 10 1 #222222

-- Feature Extraction
TEXT 50 2730 "Feature Extraction" 12 1 #1a1a1a bold

TEXT 80 2756 "For the depth-matrix condition, the Mind's Eye system converts spatial" 10 1 #222222
TEXT 50 2772 "information into structured text through orthographic raycasting. For each" 10 1 #222222
TEXT 50 2788 "scene, six depth maps (front, back, left, right, top, bottom) are generated" 10 1 #222222
TEXT 50 2804 "as character grids where each cell contains a digit 0-9 representing" 10 1 #222222
TEXT 50 2820 "normalized depth. The control condition receives only the original natural" 10 1 #222222
TEXT 50 2836 "language descriptions or VOXI source code without depth rendering." 10 1 #222222

-- Procedure
TEXT 50 2870 "Procedure" 12 1 #1a1a1a bold

TEXT 80 2896 "Each model-condition combination will be tested on all tasks. For each" 10 1 #222222
TEXT 50 2912 "task, the LLM receives the spatial problem description and (in the depth" 10 1 #222222
TEXT 50 2928 "condition) the corresponding depth matrices. The model produces an answer," 10 1 #222222
TEXT 50 2944 "which is compared against the ground truth. No iterative refinement is" 10 1 #222222
TEXT 50 2960 "permitted during benchmarking -- each answer must be given in a single pass" 10 1 #222222
TEXT 50 2976 "to ensure controlled comparison." 10 1 #222222

-- Statistical Analysis
TEXT 50 3010 "Statistical Analysis" 12 1 #1a1a1a bold

TEXT 80 3036 "A two-way analysis of variance (ANOVA) will test the main effects of" 10 1 #222222
TEXT 50 3052 "representation type and model capability, as well as their interaction." 10 1 #222222
TEXT 50 3068 "Given preliminary results suggesting that the tool helps high-capability" 10 1 #222222
TEXT 50 3084 "models but may hurt lower-capability ones, the interaction effect is of" 10 1 #222222
TEXT 50 3100 "particular theoretical interest. Post-hoc comparisons using Tukey's HSD" 10 1 #222222
TEXT 50 3116 "will identify significant pairwise differences. Effect sizes (Cohen's d)" 10 1 #222222
TEXT 50 3132 "will be reported for all significant comparisons." 10 1 #222222


